---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Demo from '../components/Demo.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Shot from '../components/Shot.astro';
---
<MarketingLayout title="Why Concise: checks before the write" description="See how Concise checks pending comments, whole-file writes, and inline PR bodies. Then it gives your agent a concrete finding to revise.">
  <header class="page-intro frame">
    <h1 data-hero>Concise checks before the write.</h1>
    <p data-hero>A prompt can ask an agent to be brief. Concise checks the text before the write runs and tells the agent what to fix.</p>
    <a class="button" href="/install/" data-hero>Install Concise <Icon name="arrow" size={18} /></a>
  </header>
  <section class="frame page-section" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="example-heading" data-reveal>Catch it before it lands.</h2><p data-reveal>Concise gives the finding, and the agent can revise. <br />Concise does not rewrite your files.</p></div>
    <Demo />
    <p class="example-disclosure">These examples are illustrations, not a live agent. No files change.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="frame page-section" aria-labelledby="defaults-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="defaults-heading" data-reveal>Three core checks.</h2><p data-reveal>These checks run without configuration. They check the submitted write or the added lines, not the whole repository.</p></div>
    <dl class="core-checks" data-reveal>
      <div><dt>Comments</dt><dd>A comment block over <strong>2 lines</strong> gets a denial with its location and the limit.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Files</dt><dd>A whole-file write or a new-file patch over <strong>300 lines</strong> gets a denial. In an ordinary update hunk, Concise checks only the added lines.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>PRs and issues</dt><dd>An inline body can have <strong>1 prose paragraph</strong> of up to <strong>3 sentences</strong>. Headings and lists are permitted.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section class="frame page-section" aria-labelledby="record-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="record-heading" data-reveal>See each decision.</h2><p data-reveal>After 2 denials on the same target, Concise allows the next attempt and flags it. The em-dash and AI-writing checks are optional and off by default.</p></div>
    <div class="shot-pair">
      <Shot view="activity" />
      <Shot view="playground" />
    </div>
    <a class="text-link section-link" href="/configuration/" data-reveal>Choose checks and exceptions <Icon name="arrow" size={17} /></a>
  </section>
  <section class="frame page-section test-feature" aria-labelledby="tests-heading">
    <div><h2 id="tests-heading" data-reveal>Quieter test output.</h2><p data-reveal>A passing test run reaches the agent as a short summary. A failed run keeps its full output. Concise saves the complete log of each run and prints its path with the summary.</p><p class="runner-list" data-reveal>pytest, go test, npm test, Jest, and Vitest</p></div>
    <div class="test-specimen" data-ui data-reveal><div class="specimen-meta"><span>Example output in Claude Code</span><span>pytest</span></div><pre><code><span class="code-muted">$ pytest tests/</span>
[filtered] runner=pytest exit=0 (cap 100)
[filtered] available output: cat '$TMPDIR/concise-test-output-hS2x6f/output.log'
[filtered] last 5 lines:
<span class="code-muted">…</span>
<span class="test-pass">========== 214 passed in 3.82s ==========</span></code></pre><div class="test-footer"><code>NOFILTER=1 pytest tests/</code><span>Bypass for one run</span></div></div>
  </section>
  <nav class="page-next frame" aria-label="Explore Concise"><a class="text-link" href="/faq/">Questions and limits <Icon name="arrow" size={17} /></a><a class="text-link" href="/use-cases/">Where it helps <Icon name="arrow" size={17} /></a></nav>
</MarketingLayout>
